module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveBundleConormal.ChartKernelTilde
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.PullbackSections.Affine
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.QuasiCoherent.TildeTensorComparison

/-!
# The generator formula for the source of the conormal map of Tag 0B3V clause 3, on a chart

`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveBundleConormal.ZeroSectionGenerator` reads the *target*
identification of [Stacks, Tag 0B3V] clause 3 on a named global section: the canonical generator
of the ideal sheaf of the zero section named by `x` goes to the section of `K^~` named by the
derivative `SymmetricAlgebra.augDeriv x` at the origin. **This file does the same for the source
identification**, whose two factors
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.restrictIsoSpecTilde` and
`Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.specModuleChartKerIso`) were pinned only by their definitions and
by naturality, never on a section.

The normalisation is the one a comparison of two identifications needs. Both halves of the
clause's chart computation land on `(ker p)^~`, and the equation that remains — that the clause's
map *is* the composite of the two — is an equation of morphisms out of a quasi-coherent sheaf on
an affine scheme, hence an equation on the global sections of `(ker p)^~`. Those sections are
generated by `AlgebraicGeometry.tilde.toOpen`, and this file says what the source identification
does to them.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.restrictIsoSelf_hom_val_app`: restricting along an
  isomorphism and back is, on sections, a presheaf restriction map.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.restrictIsoSpecTilde_inv_unit_toOpen`: **the generic
  formula.** For a quasi-coherent `F` and an affine open `U`, the inverse of the identification of
  `F|_U` with `(specModule F hU)^~` carries the global section of the pullback named by `m` —
  the unit of `(U ≅ Spec Γ(X, U))^* ⊣ (…)_*` applied to `tilde.toOpen _ ⊤ m` — to `m` itself,
  read in `Γ(F|_U, ⊤)` through the restriction map of the presheaf of `F|_U`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.restrictKernelIsoTilde_inv_unit_toOpen`: **the instance the
  clause uses.** For `k` in the kernel of the chart's linear form, the section of `(ker p)^~` named
  by `k` comes from the section of `ker(q)|_U` that `k` is, through
  `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.specModuleChartKerIso`.

## Implementation notes

Nothing is rewritten, and no composite is split at more than two folds inside a larger term:
`restrictIsoSpecTilde_inv_val_app` and `restrictKernelIsoTilde_inv_val_app` name the splits so
that the generator formulas quote them instead of performing them. See the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveBundleConormal.ChartRatio` for why no `rw` occurs on this
layer, and those of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveBundleConormal.ChartKernelTilde` for the split.

**Every morphism handed to `PresheafOfModules.congr_map_apply` and
`PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply` is written out.** Left as a metavariable, the one in the step
that reads a section of `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.specRestrict` as a section of
`F|_U` is a `(kernel) deterministic timeout`: unification has to cross
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.restrict_map`, which is a `rfl` the elaborator finds only by
unfolding the restriction along `hU.isoSpec.inv` inside a module type. With the morphism given —
`hU.isoSpec.inv.opensFunctor.map (homOfLE le_top)` — it is a direct check, and the file compiles in
seconds. The same holds of the three `eqToHom`s of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.restrictIsoSelf`.

The opens are never shown to be equal to `⊤`: each formula carries the inequality it needs as a
hypothesis (`h : ⊤ ≤ hU.isoSpec.inv ''ᵁ ⊤`), in the style of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.restrictFunctorIsoPullback_hom_val_app`. The hom-sets of
`TopologicalSpace.Opens` are subsingletons, so which proof is supplied cannot matter, and
`Subsingleton.elim` is what collapses the chains of restriction maps. The hypothesis is of course
satisfied — `hU.isoSpec.inv` is an isomorphism, so `simp` discharges it through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.image_top_eq_opensRange` — and it is left to the caller only to keep
the statements free of transport.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B3V](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B3V)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01I9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01I9)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE

variable {Y Z : Scheme.{u}}

/-- Two successive restriction maps of a presheaf of modules on opens compose to any single one
with the same source and target. -/
private theorem map_map_eq_map {T : Type*} [TopologicalSpace T]
    {R : (TopologicalSpace.Opens T)ᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat} (M : PresheafOfModules R)
    {a b c : (TopologicalSpace.Opens T)ᵒᵖ} (f : a ⟶ b) (g : b ⟶ c) (h : a ⟶ c) (y : M.obj a) :
    M.map g (M.map f y) = M.map h y :=
  (PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply M f g y).symm.trans
    (PresheafOfModules.congr_map_apply M (Subsingleton.elim _ _) y)

/-- **Restricting along an isomorphism and back is, on sections, a restriction map of the
presheaf.** `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.restrictIsoSelf` is a composite of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorComp`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorCongr` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorId`, each of which is a presheaf restriction map
along an equality of opens; the three collapse to one. -/
theorem restrictIsoSelf_hom_val_app (e : Y ≅ Z) (G : Y.Modules) (V : Y.Opens)
    (hle : V ≤ e.inv ''ᵁ (e.hom ''ᵁ V)) (y : Γ((G.restrict e.inv).restrict e.hom, V)) :
    (restrictIsoSelf e G).hom.val.app (op V) y = G.val.map (homOfLE hle).op y := by
  have h1 : (e.hom ≫ e.inv) ''ᵁ V = e.inv ''ᵁ (e.hom ''ᵁ V) := by simp
  have h2 : (𝟙 Y) ''ᵁ V = (e.hom ≫ e.inv) ''ᵁ V := by simp
  have h3 : V = (𝟙 Y) ''ᵁ V := by simp
  refine Eq.trans (rfl : (restrictIsoSelf e G).hom.val.app (op V) y =
      G.val.map (eqToHom h3).op
        (G.val.map (eqToHom h2).op (G.val.map (eqToHom h1).op y))) ?_
  exact (congrArg (G.val.map (eqToHom h3).op)
    (map_map_eq_map G.val (eqToHom h1).op (eqToHom h2).op (eqToHom (h2.trans h1)).op y)).trans
    (map_map_eq_map G.val _ _ (homOfLE hle).op y)

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
  {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)

/-- `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.restrictIsoSpecTilde` read on a global section: its
three factors, applied in turn, with the middle one — the counit of `tilde ⊣ Γ` — read at the
image of the whole chart. The split is `rfl`; naming it keeps the generator formula below from
having to perform it inside a larger term. -/
theorem restrictIsoSpecTilde_inv_val_app
    (z : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback hU.isoSpec.hom).obj (tilde (specModule F hU)), ⊤)) :
    (restrictIsoSpecTilde F hU).inv.val.app (op ⊤) z =
      (restrictIsoSelf hU.isoSpec (F.restrict U.ι)).hom.val.app (op ⊤)
        ((Scheme.Modules.fromTildeΓ (specRestrict F hU)).val.app
            (op (hU.isoSpec.hom ''ᵁ hU.isoSpec.hom ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : (Spec Γ(X, U)).Opens)))
          (((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback hU.isoSpec.hom).inv.app
              (tilde (specModule F hU))).val.app (op ⊤) z)) :=
  rfl

/-- **A quasi-coherent module is `(specModule F hU)^~` on an affine open, normalised by the
canonical global sections.** The global section of the pullback of `(specModule F hU)^~` named by
`m` — the unit of `hU.isoSpec.hom^* ⊣ (hU.isoSpec.hom)_*` applied to
`AlgebraicGeometry.tilde.toOpen _ ⊤ m` — goes back to `m` itself under
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.restrictIsoSpecTilde`.

Since those sections generate `(specModule F hU)^~` over the affine `U`, this determines the
identification: it is what makes [Stacks, Tag 01XZ] (4) *the* canonical presentation of `F|_U`
rather than one of many of its type, and it is the form in which the chart computation of
[Stacks, Tag 0B3V] clause 3 consumes it.

The three factors are discharged in turn:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback_inv_unit` undoes the crossing to the
pullback on the unit, `AlgebraicGeometry.tilde.toOpen_res` carries `toOpen` down to the image of
the chart, and `AlgebraicGeometry.TildeTensor.toOpen_fromTildeΓ_app_apply` is the counit of
`tilde ⊣ Γ` on a canonical section. What is left is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.restrictIsoSelf_hom_val_app` and one collapse of
restriction maps. -/
theorem restrictIsoSpecTilde_inv_unit_toOpen
    (h : (⊤ : (↑U : Scheme.{u}).Opens) ≤ hU.isoSpec.inv ''ᵁ ⊤) (m : specModule F hU) :
    (restrictIsoSpecTilde F hU).inv.val.app (op ⊤)
        (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction hU.isoSpec.hom).unit.app
            (tilde (specModule F hU))).val.app (op ⊤)
          (tilde.toOpen (specModule F hU) ⊤ m)) =
      (F.restrict U.ι).val.map (homOfLE h).op m := by
  have hle : (⊤ : (↑U : Scheme.{u}).Opens) ≤
      hU.isoSpec.inv ''ᵁ (hU.isoSpec.hom ''ᵁ (⊤ : (↑U : Scheme.{u}).Opens)) := by simp
  have hA : hU.isoSpec.inv ''ᵁ (hU.isoSpec.hom ''ᵁ (⊤ : (↑U : Scheme.{u}).Opens)) ≤
      hU.isoSpec.inv ''ᵁ (⊤ : (Spec Γ(X, U)).Opens) := Scheme.Hom.image_mono _ le_top
  have s1 : ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback hU.isoSpec.hom).inv.app
          (tilde (specModule F hU))).val.app (op ⊤)
        (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction hU.isoSpec.hom).unit.app
            (tilde (specModule F hU))).val.app (op ⊤)
          (tilde.toOpen (specModule F hU) ⊤ m)) =
      tilde.toOpen (specModule F hU)
        (hU.isoSpec.hom ''ᵁ hU.isoSpec.hom ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : (Spec Γ(X, U)).Opens)) m :=
    (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback_inv_unit hU.isoSpec.hom
        (tilde (specModule F hU)) ⊤ (tilde.toOpen (specModule F hU) ⊤ m)).trans
      (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
        (tilde.toOpen_res (specModule F hU) ⊤
          (hU.isoSpec.hom ''ᵁ hU.isoSpec.hom ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : (Spec Γ(X, U)).Opens))
          (homOfLE (hU.isoSpec.hom.image_preimage_le ⊤))) m)
  have s2 : (Scheme.Modules.fromTildeΓ (specRestrict F hU)).val.app
        (op (hU.isoSpec.hom ''ᵁ hU.isoSpec.hom ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : (Spec Γ(X, U)).Opens)))
        (tilde.toOpen (specModule F hU)
          (hU.isoSpec.hom ''ᵁ hU.isoSpec.hom ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : (Spec Γ(X, U)).Opens)) m) =
      (specRestrict F hU).val.map
        (homOfLE (le_top (a := hU.isoSpec.hom ''ᵁ hU.isoSpec.hom ⁻¹ᵁ
          (⊤ : (Spec Γ(X, U)).Opens)))).op m :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.TildeTensor.toOpen_fromTildeΓ_app_apply (specRestrict F hU)
      (hU.isoSpec.hom ''ᵁ hU.isoSpec.hom ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : (Spec Γ(X, U)).Opens)) m
  have s3 : (specRestrict F hU).val.map
        (homOfLE (le_top (a := hU.isoSpec.hom ''ᵁ hU.isoSpec.hom ⁻¹ᵁ
          (⊤ : (Spec Γ(X, U)).Opens)))).op m =
      (F.restrict U.ι).val.map (homOfLE hA).op m :=
    PresheafOfModules.congr_map_apply (M := (F.restrict U.ι).val)
      (f := (hU.isoSpec.inv.opensFunctor.map
        (homOfLE (le_top (a := hU.isoSpec.hom ''ᵁ hU.isoSpec.hom ⁻¹ᵁ
          (⊤ : (Spec Γ(X, U)).Opens))))).op)
      (g := (homOfLE hA).op) (Subsingleton.elim _ _) m
  refine Eq.trans (restrictIsoSpecTilde_inv_val_app F hU _) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun w =>
      (restrictIsoSelf hU.isoSpec (F.restrict U.ι)).hom.val.app (op ⊤)
        ((Scheme.Modules.fromTildeΓ (specRestrict F hU)).val.app
          (op (hU.isoSpec.hom ''ᵁ hU.isoSpec.hom ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : (Spec Γ(X, U)).Opens))) w)) s1) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun w =>
      (restrictIsoSelf hU.isoSpec (F.restrict U.ι)).hom.val.app (op ⊤) w) (s2.trans s3)) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (restrictIsoSelf_hom_val_app hU.isoSpec (F.restrict U.ι) ⊤ hle
      ((F.restrict U.ι).val.map (homOfLE hA).op m)) ?_
  exact map_map_eq_map (F.restrict U.ι).val _ _ _ m

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE

namespace Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} {E : X.Modules} (Q : Stacks.Divisors.InvertibleQuotient X E)
  (U : X.Opens) (e : Γ(Q.L, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) [E.IsQuasicoherent]
  (hU : IsAffineOpen U)

/-- `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.restrictKernelIsoTilde` read on a global section: its two
factors, applied in turn. The composite is a single `CategoryTheory.Iso.trans`, so the split is
`rfl`; naming it keeps the generator formula below from having to perform it inside a larger
term. -/
theorem restrictKernelIsoTilde_inv_val_app
    (z : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback hU.isoSpec.hom).obj (tilde (chartKerModule Q U e)), ⊤)) :
    (restrictKernelIsoTilde Q U e hU).inv.val.app (op ⊤) z =
      (restrictIsoSpecTilde (kernel Q.q) hU).inv.val.app (op ⊤)
        (((Scheme.Modules.pullback hU.isoSpec.hom).map
            ((tilde.functor Γ(X, U)).map (specModuleChartKerIso Q U e hU).inv)).val.app (op ⊤) z) :=
  rfl

/-- **The source of the conormal map of [Stacks, Tag 0B3V] clause 3, over a chart, normalised by
the canonical global sections.** The global section of `(ker p)^~` named by an element `k` of the
kernel of the chart's linear form — the unit of `hU.isoSpec.hom^* ⊣ (hU.isoSpec.hom)_*` applied to
`AlgebraicGeometry.tilde.toOpen _ ⊤ k` — comes, under
`Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.restrictKernelIsoTilde`, from the section of `ker(q)|_U` that `k`
*is*: its image under
`Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.specModuleChartKerIso`, which is
`Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.kernelSectionsKerEquiv` and hence the identity on the underlying
section of `ℰ`.

This is the source half of the normalisation the clause's chart computation needs; the target half
is `Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal.conormalZeroSectionTildeIso_hom_unit_toOpen`.

It is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.restrictIsoSpecTilde_inv_unit_toOpen` after the
module comparison has been carried across the unit, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.unit_app_val_app_naturality` together with
`AlgebraicGeometry.TildeTensor.toOpen_map_app_apply`. -/
theorem restrictKernelIsoTilde_inv_unit_toOpen
    (h : (⊤ : (↑U : Scheme.{u}).Opens) ≤ hU.isoSpec.inv ''ᵁ ⊤) (k : chartKerModule Q U e) :
    (restrictKernelIsoTilde Q U e hU).inv.val.app (op ⊤)
        (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction hU.isoSpec.hom).unit.app
            (tilde (chartKerModule Q U e))).val.app (op ⊤)
          (tilde.toOpen (chartKerModule Q U e) ⊤ k)) =
      ((kernel Q.q).restrict U.ι).val.map (homOfLE h).op
        ((specModuleChartKerIso Q U e hU).inv k) := by
  have hnat : ((Scheme.Modules.pullback hU.isoSpec.hom).map
          ((tilde.functor Γ(X, U)).map (specModuleChartKerIso Q U e hU).inv)).val.app (op ⊤)
        (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction hU.isoSpec.hom).unit.app
            (tilde (chartKerModule Q U e))).val.app (op ⊤)
          (tilde.toOpen (chartKerModule Q U e) ⊤ k)) =
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction hU.isoSpec.hom).unit.app
          (tilde (specModule (kernel Q.q) hU))).val.app (op ⊤)
        (tilde.toOpen (specModule (kernel Q.q) hU) ⊤
          ((specModuleChartKerIso Q U e hU).inv k)) :=
    (Scheme.Modules.unit_app_val_app_naturality hU.isoSpec.hom
        ((tilde.functor Γ(X, U)).map (specModuleChartKerIso Q U e hU).inv) ⊤
        (tilde.toOpen (chartKerModule Q U e) ⊤ k)).trans
      (congrArg (fun w =>
          ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction hU.isoSpec.hom).unit.app
            (tilde (specModule (kernel Q.q) hU))).val.app (op ⊤) w)
        (AlgebraicGeometry.TildeTensor.toOpen_map_app_apply
          (specModuleChartKerIso Q U e hU).inv ⊤ k))
  refine Eq.trans (restrictKernelIsoTilde_inv_val_app Q U e hU _) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun w =>
      (restrictIsoSpecTilde (kernel Q.q) hU).inv.val.app (op ⊤) w) hnat) ?_
  exact restrictIsoSpecTilde_inv_unit_toOpen (kernel Q.q) hU h
    ((specModuleChartKerIso Q U e hU).inv k)

end Stacks.ProjectiveBundleConormal

end
